        "original_id": "17aa85aa-82e5-5dc4-be22-7d57ba835fad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: RZA, Eli Roth, Bob Perry, Quentin Tarantino\n- Films: The Man with the Iron Fists, Inglourious Basterds\n- Organizations: Soul Temple Records\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, actor\n- Awards: SAG Award, BFCA Critic's Choice Award\n\nFacts:\n- Eli Roth was born on April 18, 1972, and he is an American film director, producer, writer, and actor.\n- Eli Roth's most prominent acting role was Donny \"The Bear Jew\" Donowitz in Quentin Tarantino's war film Inglourious Basterds.\n- Eli Roth won a SAG Award for Best Ensemble and a BFCA Critic's Choice Award for Best Acting Ensemble for Inglourious Basterds.\n- The Man with the Iron Fists is a 2012 American martial arts film directed by RZA and written by RZA and Eli Roth.\n- Soul Temple Records is an American record label founded in 2012 by RZA and Bob Perry after the release of The Man with the Iron Fists.",
